    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-3-10",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod3-Q10",
        "itemBody": "<p>Investor A and Investor B invest in a fund for two years: Year 1 Year 2 Fund Return Positive Negative Portfolio Money-Weighted Rate of Return Investor A 7.5% Investor B 8.2% Given the information in the table, which of the following is least likely to be an explanation for the difference between the two money-weighted rates of return?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "2a410ff1-e11f-4b24-9984-b6010a36ed6b",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. Investor A increased the investment in the fund at the end of year 1 whereas investor B did not make any additions or withdrawals</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "bc93710f-32dd-43bc-9073-ae9ca5e6a71a",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. Investor B decreased the investment in the fund at the end of year 1 whereas investor A did not make any additions or withdrawals</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "8b8cd79f-e1ef-4f91-a967-5b3cebd93cbb",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. The investors invested different amounts at inception and afterward did not make any additions or withdrawals</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "scoringData": {
          "value": "2a410ff1-e11f-4b24-9984-b6010a36ed6b"
